WHEREAS, the Georgia General Assembly passed a local act incorporating the Town of Clermont, Georgia, being approved May 6, 2015, and being Georgia laws 2015, p. 3767, et seq., and which established in said charter certain Councilmember wards and certain residency requirements for election upon the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia;

WHEREAS, the Georgia General Assembly, by local act approved on May 3, 2018, and being Georgia Laws 2018, pp. 3610, et seq., amended the Councilmember wards that established the election. wards for Councilmembers, and clarified the description of said wards;

WHEREAS, 0.C.G.A. § 36-35-4.1(b) authorizes the Town Council for the Town of Clermont, Georgia to reapportion the election districts a/k/a wards from which members of the municipal governing authority are elected following publication of the United States decennial census of 1980 or any future such census;

WHEREAS, the United States decennial census of 2020 has been completed, and the census data published, which reflects certain population changes within the Town of Clermont, Georgia, and which necessitates the reapportionment of the election districts a/k/a wards from which members of the Clermont Town Council are elected;

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia, has utilized services of persons knowledgeable in the drafting of election districts to comply with the requirements of 0.C.G.A. § 36-35-4.1(b), and has determined new districts a/k/a wards that comply with said requirements; and

